- Many developers incorrectly treat retrieval recall and ANN recall as the same metric.
- Semantic retrieval recall Measures whether retrieved documents are actually relevant to the user's question.
- \[ Recall@K=\frac{ R K\cap G }{ G } \] Where \(G\) contains human-annotated relevant documents.
- ANN recall Measures whether approximate search returns the same neighbors as exact vector search.
- \[ ANNRecall@K= \frac{ ANN K\cap Exact K }{K} \] These metrics answer different questions.
- Actual performance must be benchmarked using your corpus and hardware.

